# Claude Enterprise re-seed / skill install reminder

Claude Enterprise does not pick up repo edits automatically. After work that changes what CE serves, **end the response with a short deploy reminder** naming only what actually changed.

## When to remind

**Re-seed project** (delete `project-files/` in CE, upload fresh from `mpr-project/project-files/`):
- Any file under `mpr-project/project-files/` changed (inventory, assignment, tags HTML, CLAUDE/ROUTING/skills docs that ship in the upload, etc.)
- After merging `/updates/` session-updates into project-files

**Reinstall skill(s)** (rebuild `.skill` zip, upload/replace in CE):
- Any change under `skills/SKILL-00N-*/` (especially `SKILL.md` or `manifest.json` version bump)
- Packaging/layout fixes that affect the zip CE mounts

## When not to remind

- Docs or tooling that never upload (`UPDATE-PROCESS.md`, `generate-tags.js`, `tags-template.html` alone — unless `mpr-tags.html` was regenerated)
- Pure local investigation with no durable CE-facing edits
- Reminder already given in this turn for the same changes

## Reminder format (keep short)

```
CE deploy still needed:
- Re-seed project-files (…list why if helpful…)
- Rebuild/reinstall SKILL-00N … (version x.y.z)
```

Omit the bullet that does not apply. Do not invent packaging steps the user did not ask for — just flag that CE is stale until they re-seed / reinstall.

